  "source": "BofA Securities",
  "title": "UnitedHealth Group: Takes from call: new guide a good base for thinking about 2027 EPS",
  "type": "equity_research",
  "priority": "medium",
  "published": "2026-07-16",
  "insights": [
   "UnitedHealth Group's guidance raise is viewed as a strong base for 2027 EPS, with the company signaling high earnings quality and a $19.50-$20.00 base for 2027 forecasting.",
   "The company remains bullish on its long-term 13-16% growth algorithm, driven by core business growth, productivity gains, and capital deployment.",
   "Medicare Advantage (MA) margins are expected to finish above 3% in 2026, with member retention performing better than anticipated despite a 1.1 million member decline.",
   "Commercial cost trends are under pressure, exceeding the 11% expectation due to Independent Dispute Resolution (IDR) process costs, higher acuity/provider coding, and specialty drug costs.",
   "Optum Health is outperforming with recontracting efforts substantially complete and AI ambient listening technology rolled out to 70% of doctors.",
   "Medicaid margins remain pressured for 2026 despite medical management initiatives, with rate actions on 80% of revenue aiming to get margins on track for 6-7%."
  ],
  "market_movers": [
   {
    "ticker": "UNH",
    "action": "reiterate",
    "rating": "Buy",
    "price_target": "$475.00",
    "rationale": "Turnaround is happening faster than expected, with strong earnings quality and a solid long-term growth algorithm.",
    "conviction": "medium"
   }
  ],
